WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:08.450
Some stands, like the portable carts, have no stand lead. After your shift, you log your own time. It takes about a minute.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:14.570
A few hours before your shift, you get an email: Log your hours, with your stand and the date.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:19.400
This stand has no stand lead, so when your shift is over, you log your own time.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.147
Clock in no more than fifteen minutes before your start. Earlier times get flagged for review.

00:00:25.347 --> 00:00:30.120
After your shift, tap Log stand hours. The link is yours alone.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:34.427
The page shows your stand, the date, and your scheduled time.

00:00:34.627 --> 00:00:38.730
Moved to a different stand at the game? Change Stand worked.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:44.722
Your scheduled times are filled in. Change them to when you actually clocked in and out.

00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:49.253
Check who your hours count for: your student's full name, or General fund.

00:00:49.453 --> 00:00:52.590
And the program. It's filled in from your student's record.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:57.940
Someone else worked your spot? Tap Someone else worked this shift, and type who did.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:02.439
A photo is optional. These stands don't have a sign-in sheet.

00:01:02.639 --> 00:01:04.538
Your name is already filled in.

00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:07.448
Want a copy of what you sent? Add your email.

00:01:07.648 --> 00:01:13.780
Tap Submit for approval. Your hours are added after the IU liaison approves them.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:20.590
Done. Need to fix something? Open the same link again, and resubmit before it's approved.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:30.410
Log your time as soon as your shift ends, while you still remember it. Forgot? You'll get one reminder email the next day, with the same link.
